Ladybird keeps a document’s fetch records reachable while their fetches
run, so that aborting the document as it unloads reaches every fetch
still in flight. In Blink, the FetchManager traces each in-flight
fetch’s Loader in its loaders_ set, and FetchManager::ContextDestroyed()
disposes of each one, canceling its request. WebKit’s FetchResponse and
XMLHttpRequest are ActiveDOMObjects, whose stop() the document calls as
it stops, and XMLHttpRequest::stop() aborts the request. And Gecko’s
XMLHttpRequestMainThread::DisconnectFromOwner() aborts the request as
soon as its window goes away.
